{"format":"bench-library","formatVersion":1,"id":"motion-sensors","name":"Motion sensors","version":"1.0.0","author":"Bench Workshop","owner":"codeopen0-cpu","description":"Sensors that feel how they move and which way they face: a tilt switch, a compass (QMC5883L, as on the GY-271) and an ADXL345 accelerometer. They feel the real motion of whatever they're glued to: pick it up with the hand and tilt it. Also sketch libraries for the app's own MPU-6050 (Adafruit_MPU6050.h and MPU6050.h), and a self-balancing robot to build on.","category":"Sensors","needsApp":"0.4.0","code":"// Motion sensors: they read part.motion(), how the part they're on moves and turns (the app works it\n// out from the physics). Axes as on the boards: x along the board, y away from the pins (the part's\n// -z), z up (the part's +y).\nconst chip = (m) => ({ x: m.accel[0], y: -m.accel[2], z: m.accel[1] });\n/** a world direction in the part's own frame (rotate by the inverse of its orientation) */\nconst rotInv = ([x, y, z, w], [vx, vy, vz]) => {\n  // rotate by the conjugate (-x, -y, -z, w): v + 2w(u x v) + 2u x (u x v), u = (-x, -y, -z)\n  const ux = -x, uy = -y, uz = -z;\n  const tx = 2 * (uy * vz - uz * vy), ty = 2 * (uz * vx - ux * vz), tz = 2 * (ux * vy - uy * vx);\n  return [vx + w * tx + (uy * tz - uz * ty), vy + w * ty + (uz * tx - ux * tz), vz + w * tz + (ux * ty - uy * tx)];\n};\n\n// Tilt switch: a ball in a tube. Upright (pins down) it rests on the contacts: DO LOW.\nbench.device('tilt', (part) => {\n  let powered = false, closed = true;\n  return {\n    step(io) {\n      const v = io.supply('VCC', 'GND');\n      powered = v >= 2.5;\n      const m = part.motion();\n      // (closed while \"up\" is within ~45 degrees of the part's own up: up[1] = cos(tilt))\n      closed = m.up[1] > 0.7;\n      if (!powered) { io.release('DO'); io.draw(0); return; }\n      io.drive('DO', closed ? 0 : v, 1);\n      io.draw(closed ? 0.0005 : 0.0001);\n    },\n    status() {\n      if (!powered) return ['no power'];\n      return [closed ? 'upright: switch closed (DO LOW)' : 'tilted: switch open (DO HIGH)'];\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n// QMC5883L: registers 0x00-0x05 X, Y, Z (16-bit, low byte first), 0x06 status (bit 0: new data),\n// 0x09 control (bits 0-1 mode: 01 = continuous; bits 4-5 range: 00 = 2 G, 12000 LSB/G),\n// 0x0B set/reset period, 0x0D chip id 0xFF.\n// The Earth's field on the bench: 0.2 gauss towards north (-z) and 0.45 gauss down.\nbench.device('qmc5883l', (part) => {\n  const regs = new Array(256).fill(0);\n  regs[0x0d] = 0xff;\n  let powered = false, ptr = 0, reads = 0, heading = 0;\n  // the Earth's field (world: north -z, down -y) as the chip feels it: turned into the part's frame\n  const field = (m) => {\n    const [qx, qy, qz, qw] = m.quat;\n    const v = rotInv([qx, qy, qz, qw], [0, -0.45, -0.2]);\n    return { x: v[0], y: -v[2], z: v[1] }; // (chip axes: x, y away from the pins, z up)\n  };\n  return {\n    i2c: {\n      address: () => (powered ? 0x0d : -1),\n      write(bytes) {\n        if (!bytes.length) return true;\n        ptr = bytes[0];\n        for (let i = 1; i < bytes.length; i++) regs[(ptr + i - 1) & 255] = bytes[i];\n        return true;\n      },\n      read(n) {\n        reads++;\n        const out = [];\n        for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) out.push(regs[(ptr + i) & 255]);\n        if (ptr <= 0x05 && ptr + n > 0x05) regs[0x06] &= ~1; // (reading the data clears \"new data\")\n        return out;\n      },\n    },\n    step(io) {\n      powered = io.supply('VCC', 'GND') >= 2.2;\n      if (!powered) { io.release('DRDY'); io.draw(0); return; }\n      const m = part.motion();\n      heading = m.heading;\n      const continuous = (regs[0x09] & 3) === 1;\n      if (continuous) {\n        const lsb = (regs[0x09] & 0x30) ? 3000 : 12000;\n        const b = field(m);\n        const s16 = (x) => Math.max(-32768, Math.min(32767, Math.round(x * lsb))) & 0xffff;\n        [b.x, b.y, b.z].forEach((v, i) => { const w = s16(v); regs[i * 2] = w & 255; regs[i * 2 + 1] = w >> 8; });\n        regs[0x06] |= 1;\n      }\n      io.drive('DRDY', regs[0x06] & 1 ? io.supply('VCC', 'GND') : 0, 1);\n      io.draw(continuous ? 0.0026 : 0.00003);\n    },\n    status() {\n      if (!powered) return ['no power'];\n      if ((regs[0x09] & 3) !== 1) return ['standby (the program hasn\\'t started it: compass.init())', `${reads} reads`];\n      return [`facing ${Math.round(heading) % 360} deg (its arrow: 0 north, 90 east)`, `${reads} reads`];\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n// ADXL345: 0x00 device id 0xE5, 0x2D POWER_CTL (bit 3 measure), 0x31 DATA_FORMAT (bits 0-1 range,\n// bit 3 full resolution), 0x32-0x37 X, Y, Z (16-bit, low byte first). Full resolution: 256 LSB/g.\nbench.device('adxl345', (part) => {\n  const regs = new Array(64).fill(0);\n  regs[0x00] = 0xe5;\n  regs[0x2c] = 0x0a;\n  let powered = false, ptr = 0, reads = 0, g = { x: 0, y: 0, z: 1 };\n  return {\n    i2c: {\n      address: () => (powered ? 0x53 : -1),\n      write(bytes) {\n        if (!bytes.length) return true;\n        ptr = bytes[0] & 63;\n        for (let i = 1; i < bytes.length; i++) regs[(ptr + i - 1) & 63] = bytes[i];\n        return true;\n      },\n      read(n) {\n        reads++;\n        const out = [];\n        for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) out.push(regs[(ptr + i) & 63]);\n        return out;\n      },\n    },\n    step(io) {\n      powered = io.supply('VCC', 'GND') >= 2;\n      if (!powered) { io.draw(0); return; }\n      g = chip(part.motion());\n      const measuring = regs[0x2d] & 0x08;\n      const range = regs[0x31] & 3, full = regs[0x31] & 0x08;\n      const lsb = full ? 256 : 256 / (1 << range);\n      const lim = full ? 4096 * (1 << range) / 4 : 512;\n      [g.x, g.y, g.z].forEach((v, i) => {\n        const w = measuring ? Math.max(-lim, Math.min(lim - 1, Math.round(v * lsb))) & 0xffff : 0;\n        regs[0x32 + i * 2] = w & 255;\n        regs[0x33 + i * 2] = w >> 8;\n      });\n      io.draw(measuring ? 0.00014 : 0.0000001);\n    },\n    status() {\n      if (!powered) return ['no power'];\n      if (!(regs[0x2d] & 0x08)) return ['standby (POWER_CTL measure bit not set: accel.begin())'];\n      return [`x ${g.x.toFixed(2)} g, y ${g.y.toFixed(2)} g, z ${g.z.toFixed(2)} g`, `${reads} reads`];\n    },\n  };\n});\n","sketch":{"Adafruit_MPU6050.h":{"classes":["Adafruit_MPU6050","sensors_event_t"],"exports":["MPU6050_RANGE_2_G","MPU6050_RANGE_4_G","MPU6050_RANGE_8_G","MPU6050_RANGE_16_G","MPU6050_RANGE_250_DEG","MPU6050_RANGE_500_DEG","MPU6050_RANGE_1000_DEG","MPU6050_RANGE_2000_DEG","MPU6050_BAND_260_HZ","MPU6050_BAND_184_HZ","MPU6050_BAND_94_HZ","MPU6050_BAND_44_HZ","MPU6050_BAND_21_HZ","MPU6050_BAND_10_HZ","MPU6050_BAND_5_HZ","SENSORS_GRAVITY_STANDARD"],"code":"// Adafruit_MPU6050.h for the app's MPU-6050 module (I2C 0x68):\n//   Adafruit_MPU6050 mpu;  mpu.begin();  sensors_event_t a, g, temp;  mpu.getEvent(&a, &g, &temp);\n//   a.acceleration.x (m/s2), g.gyro.x (rad/s), temp.temperature (C)\nclass sensors_event_t {\n  constructor() {\n    this.acceleration = { x: 0, y: 0, z: 0 };\n    this.gyro = { x: 0, y: 0, z: 0 };\n    this.magnetic = { x: 0, y: 0, z: 0 };\n    this.temperature = 0;\n    this.timestamp = 0;\n  }\n}\nconst SENSORS_GRAVITY_STANDARD = 9.80665;\nconst MPU6050_RANGE_2_G = 0, MPU6050_RANGE_4_G = 1, MPU6050_RANGE_8_G = 2, MPU6050_RANGE_16_G = 3;\nconst MPU6050_RANGE_250_DEG = 0, MPU6050_RANGE_500_DEG = 1, MPU6050_RANGE_1000_DEG = 2, MPU6050_RANGE_2000_DEG = 3;\nconst MPU6050_BAND_260_HZ = 0, MPU6050_BAND_184_HZ = 1, MPU6050_BAND_94_HZ = 2, MPU6050_BAND_44_HZ = 3, MPU6050_BAND_21_HZ = 4, MPU6050_BAND_10_HZ = 5, MPU6050_BAND_5_HZ = 6;\n\nclass Adafruit_MPU6050 {\n  constructor() { this.addr = 0x68; this.arange = 0; this.grange = 0; this.band = 0; }\n  _w(reg, v) { Wire.beginTransmission(this.addr); Wire.write(reg); Wire.write(v); return Wire.endTransmission() === 0; }\n  _r(reg, n) {\n    Wire.beginTransmission(this.addr); Wire.write(reg);\n    if (Wire.endTransmission() !== 0) return null;\n    if (Wire.requestFrom(this.addr, n) < n) return null;\n    const out = [];\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) out.push(Wire.read());\n    return out;\n  }\n  begin(addr = 0x68) {\n    this.addr = addr;\n    const id = this._r(0x75, 1);\n    if (!id || id[0] !== 0x68) return false;\n    this._w(0x6b, 0x00); // wake up\n    this.setAccelerometerRange(this.arange);\n    this.setGyroRange(this.grange);\n    return true;\n  }\n  setAccelerometerRange(r) { this.arange = r & 3; this._w(0x1c, this.arange << 3); }\n  getAccelerometerRange() { return this.arange; }\n  setGyroRange(r) { this.grange = r & 3; this._w(0x1b, this.grange << 3); }\n  getGyroRange() { return this.grange; }\n  setFilterBandwidth(b) { this.band = b; this._w(0x1a, b & 7); }\n  getFilterBandwidth() { return this.band; }\n  setSampleRateDivisor() {}\n  enableSleep(on) { this._w(0x6b, on ? 0x40 : 0); }\n  /** fills a (m/s2), g (rad/s) and temp (C) */\n  getEvent(a, g, temp) {\n    const d = this._r(0x3b, 14);\n    if (!d) return false;\n    const s = (i) => { const v = (d[i] << 8) | d[i + 1]; return v >= 32768 ? v - 65536 : v; };\n    const aLsb = 16384 / (1 << this.arange), gLsb = 131 / (1 << this.grange);\n    const t = millis();\n    if (a) { a.acceleration.x = (s(0) / aLsb) * SENSORS_GRAVITY_STANDARD; a.acceleration.y = (s(2) / aLsb) * SENSORS_GRAVITY_STANDARD; a.acceleration.z = (s(4) / aLsb) * SENSORS_GRAVITY_STANDARD; a.timestamp = t; }\n    if (temp) { temp.temperature = s(6) / 340 + 36.53; temp.timestamp = t; }\n    if (g) { g.gyro.x = ((s(8) / gLsb) * PI) / 180; g.gyro.y = ((s(10) / gLsb) * PI) / 180; g.gyro.z = ((s(12) / gLsb) * PI) / 180; g.timestamp = t; }\n    return true;\n  }\n}\n"},"Adafruit_Sensor.h":{"classes":["sensors_event_t"],"code":"// Adafruit_Sensor.h: the \"unified sensor\" event the Adafruit libraries fill in.\n//   sensors_event_t e;  e.acceleration.x (m/s2), e.gyro.x (rad/s), e.magnetic.x (uT), e.temperature (C)\nclass sensors_event_t {\n  constructor() {\n    this.acceleration = { x: 0, y: 0, z: 0 };\n    this.gyro = { x: 0, y: 0, z: 0 };\n    this.magnetic = { x: 0, y: 0, z: 0 };\n    this.temperature = 0;\n    this.timestamp = 0;\n    this.sensor_id = 0;\n    this.type = 0;\n  }\n}\n"},"MPU6050.h":{"classes":["MPU6050"],"exports":["MPU6050_ACCEL_FS_2","MPU6050_ACCEL_FS_4","MPU6050_ACCEL_FS_8","MPU6050_ACCEL_FS_16","MPU6050_GYRO_FS_250","MPU6050_GYRO_FS_500","MPU6050_GYRO_FS_1000","MPU6050_GYRO_FS_2000"],"code":"// MPU6050.h (the i2cdevlib / Electronic Cats style) for the app's MPU-6050 module (I2C 0x68):\n//   MPU6050 mpu;  mpu.initialize();  mpu.testConnection();\n//   int16_t ax, ay, az, gx, gy, gz;  mpu.getMotion6(&ax, &ay, &az, &gx, &gy, &gz);  (raw: 16384 = 1 g, 131 = 1 deg/s)\nconst MPU6050_ACCEL_FS_2 = 0, MPU6050_ACCEL_FS_4 = 1, MPU6050_ACCEL_FS_8 = 2, MPU6050_ACCEL_FS_16 = 3;\nconst MPU6050_GYRO_FS_250 = 0, MPU6050_GYRO_FS_500 = 1, MPU6050_GYRO_FS_1000 = 2, MPU6050_GYRO_FS_2000 = 3;\n\nclass MPU6050 {\n  constructor(addr = 0x68) { this.addr = addr; }\n  _w(reg, v) { Wire.beginTransmission(this.addr); Wire.write(reg); Wire.write(v); return Wire.endTransmission() === 0; }\n  _r(reg, n) {\n    Wire.beginTransmission(this.addr); Wire.write(reg);\n    if (Wire.endTransmission() !== 0) return null;\n    if (Wire.requestFrom(this.addr, n) < n) return null;\n    const out = [];\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) out.push(Wire.read());\n    return out;\n  }\n  initialize() { this._w(0x6b, 0x00); this._w(0x1b, 0); this._w(0x1c, 0); }\n  testConnection() { const id = this._r(0x75, 1); return !!id && id[0] === 0x68; }\n  getDeviceID() { const id = this._r(0x75, 1); return id ? id[0] >> 1 : 0; }\n  setFullScaleAccelRange(r) { this._w(0x1c, (r & 3) << 3); }\n  setFullScaleGyroRange(r) { this._w(0x1b, (r & 3) << 3); }\n  setDLPFMode(m) { this._w(0x1a, m & 7); }\n  setSleepEnabled(on) { this._w(0x6b, on ? 0x40 : 0); }\n  _raw() {\n    const d = this._r(0x3b, 14);\n    if (!d) return [0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0];\n    const out = [];\n    for (let i = 0; i < 14; i += 2) { const v = (d[i] << 8) | d[i + 1]; out.push(v >= 32768 ? v - 65536 : v); }\n    return out;\n  }\n  /** all six at once into the variables handed over: getMotion6(&ax, &ay, &az, &gx, &gy, &gz) */\n  getMotion6(ax, ay, az, gx, gy, gz) {\n    const r = this._raw();\n    setRef(ax, r[0]); setRef(ay, r[1]); setRef(az, r[2]); setRef(gx, r[4]); setRef(gy, r[5]); setRef(gz, r[6]);\n  }\n  getAcceleration(ax, ay, az) { const r = this._raw(); setRef(ax, r[0]); setRef(ay, r[1]); setRef(az, r[2]); }\n  getRotation(gx, gy, gz) { const r = this._raw(); setRef(gx, r[4]); setRef(gy, r[5]); setRef(gz, r[6]); }\n  getAccelerationX() { return this._raw()[0]; }\n  getAccelerationY() { return this._raw()[1]; }\n  getAccelerationZ() { return this._raw()[2]; }\n  getRotationX() { return this._raw()[4]; }\n  getRotationY() { return this._raw()[5]; }\n  getRotationZ() { return this._raw()[6]; }\n  getTemperature() { return this._raw()[3]; }\n}\n"},"Adafruit_ADXL345_U.h":{"classes":["Adafruit_ADXL345_Unified","sensors_event_t"],"exports":["ADXL345_RANGE_2_G","ADXL345_RANGE_4_G","ADXL345_RANGE_8_G","ADXL345_RANGE_16_G","SENSORS_GRAVITY_STANDARD"],"code":"// Adafruit_ADXL345_U.h: Adafruit_ADXL345_Unified accel(12345);  accel.begin();\n//   accel.setRange(ADXL345_RANGE_16_G);  sensors_event_t e;  accel.getEvent(&e);  e.acceleration.x (m/s2)\nclass sensors_event_t {\n  constructor() {\n    this.acceleration = { x: 0, y: 0, z: 0 };\n    this.gyro = { x: 0, y: 0, z: 0 };\n    this.magnetic = { x: 0, y: 0, z: 0 };\n    this.temperature = 0;\n    this.timestamp = 0;\n  }\n}\nconst SENSORS_GRAVITY_STANDARD = 9.80665;\nconst ADXL345_RANGE_2_G = 0, ADXL345_RANGE_4_G = 1, ADXL345_RANGE_8_G = 2, ADXL345_RANGE_16_G = 3;\n\nclass Adafruit_ADXL345_Unified {\n  constructor(id = -1) { this.id = id; this.addr = 0x53; this.range = ADXL345_RANGE_2_G; }\n  _w(reg, v) { Wire.beginTransmission(this.addr); Wire.write(reg); Wire.write(v); return Wire.endTransmission() === 0; }\n  _r(reg, n) {\n    Wire.beginTransmission(this.addr); Wire.write(reg);\n    if (Wire.endTransmission() !== 0) return null;\n    if (Wire.requestFrom(this.addr, n) < n) return null;\n    const out = [];\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) out.push(Wire.read());\n    return out;\n  }\n  begin(addr = 0x53) {\n    this.addr = addr;\n    const id = this._r(0x00, 1);\n    if (!id || id[0] !== 0xe5) return false;\n    this._w(0x2d, 0x08); // measure\n    this.setRange(this.range);\n    return true;\n  }\n  setRange(r) { this.range = r & 3; this._w(0x31, 0x08 | this.range); } // (full resolution: 4 mg per step)\n  getRange() { return this.range; }\n  setDataRate() {}\n  getDeviceID() { const id = this._r(0x00, 1); return id ? id[0] : 0; }\n  _xyz() {\n    const d = this._r(0x32, 6);\n    if (!d) return [0, 0, 0];\n    return [0, 2, 4].map((i) => { const v = d[i] | (d[i + 1] << 8); return v >= 32768 ? v - 65536 : v; });\n  }\n  getX() { return this._xyz()[0]; }\n  getY() { return this._xyz()[1]; }\n  getZ() { return this._xyz()[2]; }\n  getEvent(e) {\n    const [x, y, z] = this._xyz();\n    const k = 0.004 * SENSORS_GRAVITY_STANDARD; // (full resolution: 4 mg per step at any range)\n    e.acceleration.x = x * k; e.acceleration.y = y * k; e.acceleration.z = z * k;\n    e.timestamp = millis();\n    return true;\n  }\n}\n"},"QMC5883LCompass.h":{"classes":["QMC5883LCompass"],"code":"// QMC5883LCompass.h (MPrograms' library): QMC5883LCompass compass;  compass.init();\n//   compass.read();  compass.getX() / getY() / getZ();  compass.getAzimuth() (degrees, -180..180 as the\n//   real one gives it: 0 north, 90 east);  compass.getBearing(az) (0-15);  compass.getDirection(buf, az)\nclass QMC5883LCompass {\n  constructor() { this.addr = 0x0d; this.v = [0, 0, 0]; this.decl = 0; this.cal = null; }\n  _w(reg, v) { Wire.beginTransmission(this.addr); Wire.write(reg); Wire.write(v); return Wire.endTransmission() === 0; }\n  init() {\n    this._w(0x0b, 0x01); // set/reset period\n    this._w(0x09, 0x1d); // as the real init(): continuous, 200 Hz, 8 G range, oversampling 512\n  }\n  setADDR(a) { this.addr = a; }\n  setMode(mode, odr, rng, osr) { this._w(0x09, (mode | odr | rng | osr) & 255); }\n  setMagneticDeclination(deg, min = 0) { this.decl = deg + min / 60; }\n  setCalibration() {}\n  setCalibrationOffsets() {}\n  setCalibrationScales() {}\n  setSmoothing() {}\n  read() {\n    Wire.beginTransmission(this.addr); Wire.write(0x00);\n    if (Wire.endTransmission() !== 0) return;\n    if (Wire.requestFrom(this.addr, 6) < 6) return;\n    const d = [];\n    for (let i = 0; i < 6; i++) d.push(Wire.read());\n    this.v = [0, 2, 4].map((i) => { const x = d[i] | (d[i + 1] << 8); return x >= 32768 ? x - 65536 : x; });\n  }\n  getX() { return this.v[0]; }\n  getY() { return this.v[1]; }\n  getZ() { return this.v[2]; }\n  getAzimuth() {\n    let a = (Math.atan2(this.v[1], this.v[0]) * 180) / Math.PI + this.decl;\n    if (a > 180) a -= 360;\n    return Math.round(a);\n  }\n  /** 0-15: N, NNE, NE ... */\n  getBearing(az) { return Math.round((((az % 360) + 360) % 360) / 22.5) % 16; }\n  /** the 3-letter direction (\"NNE\") into a char[3] buffer handed over (or returned) */\n  getDirection(buf, az) {\n    const names = ['N', 'NNE', 'NE', 'ENE', 'E', 'ESE', 'SE', 'SSE', 'S', 'SSW', 'SW', 'WSW', 'W', 'WNW', 'NW', 'NNW'];\n    const s = names[this.getBearing(az)].padEnd(3, ' ');\n    if (isRef(buf)) setRef(buf, s);\n    else if (buf && typeof buf === 'object') for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) buf[i] = s[i];\n    return s;\n  }\n}\n"}},"parts":[{"id":"tilt-switch","name":"Tilt switch (SW-520D module)","description":"A tiny ball in a tube: upright (pins down), the ball closes the switch and DO is LOW; tip it more than about 45 degrees and DO goes HIGH. VCC (3.3-5 V), GND, DO. Glue it to something and tilt that, or carry it with the hand and turn it over.","swatch":"#1f5fbf","mass":2,"shape":[{"box":[1.5,0.16,3],"at":[0,0.08,0],"color":"#1f5fbf"},{"cyl":[0.3,1.1],"at":[0,0.4,0.6],"rot":[90,0,0],"color":"#2a2a2c"},{"box":[0.2,0.1,0.2],"at":[0.45,0.21,-0.4],"color":"#e33030","collide":false}],"pinRows":[{"ids":["VCC","GND","DO"],"at":[-0.254,0,-1.3],"kinds":{"VCC":"vin","GND":"gnd","DO":"out"},"extra":{"VCC":{"label":"VCC (3.3-5 V)","vmin":3,"vmax":5.5}}}],"device":"tilt"},{"id":"compass","name":"Compass (QMC5883L, GY-271)","description":"A 3-axis magnetic sensor: it feels the Earth's field, so it knows which way it faces (north is away from you on the bench: the -z direction). I2C at 0x0D. VCC (3.3-5 V), GND, SCL, SDA. #include <QMC5883LCompass.h>; compass.init(); compass.read(); compass.getAzimuth() (0 north, 90 east: the way its +x side, the arrow, points).","swatch":"#2a2d8f","mass":2,"shape":[{"box":[1.4,0.16,1.8],"at":[0,0.08,0],"color":"#2a2d8f"},{"box":[0.3,0.1,0.3],"at":[0,0.21,0.3],"color":"#141416"},{"box":[0.8,0.01,0.12],"at":[0,0.165,0.7],"color":"#f2f2f2","collide":false},{"box":[0.12,0.01,0.3],"at":[0.35,0.165,0.62],"rot":[0,45,0],"color":"#f2f2f2","collide":false}],"pinRows":[{"ids":["VCC","GND","SCL","SDA","DRDY"],"at":[-0.508,0,-0.75],"kinds":{"VCC":"vin","GND":"gnd","SCL":"i2c","SDA":"i2c","DRDY":"out"},"extra":{"VCC":{"label":"VCC (3.3-5 V)","vmin":2.2,"vmax":5.5}}}],"device":"qmc5883l"},{"id":"adxl345","name":"Accelerometer (ADXL345)","description":"A 3-axis accelerometer (I2C at 0x53): it feels gravity (1 g down when still) and every shake. VCC (3.3-5 V), GND, SDA, SCL. #include <Adafruit_ADXL345_U.h>; Adafruit_ADXL345_Unified accel(12345); accel.begin(); sensors_event_t e; accel.getEvent(&e); e.acceleration.x (m/s2). Axes: x along the board, y away from the pins, z up.","swatch":"#6a2fb0","mass":2,"shape":[{"box":[1.8,0.16,2.6],"at":[0,0.08,0],"color":"#6a2fb0"},{"box":[0.5,0.1,0.5],"at":[0,0.21,0.4],"color":"#141416"}],"pinRows":[{"ids":["GND","VCC","CS","INT1","INT2","SDO","SDA","SCL"],"at":[-0.889,0,-1.1],"kinds":{"GND":"gnd","VCC":"vin","CS":"in","INT1":"out","INT2":"out","SDO":"in","SDA":"i2c","SCL":"i2c"},"extra":{"VCC":{"label":"VCC (3.3-5 V)","vmin":2,"vmax":5.5},"CS":{"pulled":"up"},"SDO":{"pulled":"down"}}}],"device":"adxl345"}],"examples":[{"name":"Self-balancing robot","description":"Two wheels and a tall body that would fall over: the board reads the MPU-6050 and drives the motors to keep it upright (a PID loop). Press Run, then push it with the hand (Shift) and watch it catch itself; the serial monitor's Plot shows the angle.","project":{"format":"bench-workshop","version":1,"name":"Self-balancing robot","parts":[{"uid":"chassis","type":"plate","name":"Chassis","params":{"w":7,"h":0.3,"d":9,"material":"plastic","color":"#8fa3b8"},"parent":null,"pos":[0,4.4,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"motorR","type":"motor-tt","name":"Right motor","params":{},"parent":{"uid":"chassis","body":"body"},"pos":[-1.6,-0.15,3.55],"rot":[0,0,1,0]},{"uid":"motorL","type":"motor-tt","name":"Left motor","params":{},"parent":{"uid":"chassis","body":"body"},"pos":[1.6,-0.15,-3.55],"rot":[1,0,0,0]},{"uid":"wheelR","type":"wheel","name":"Right wheel","params":{"r":3.3,"width":2.6,"grip":1.4},"parent":{"uid":"motorR","body":"hub"},"pos":[0,0.45,0],"rot":[0,1,0,0]},{"uid":"wheelL","type":"wheel","name":"Left wheel","params":{"r":3.3,"width":2.6,"grip":1.4},"parent":{"uid":"motorL","body":"hub"},"pos":[0,0.45,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"mastF","type":"block","name":"Mast","params":{"w":1.2,"h":12,"d":0.8,"material":"plastic","color":"#d8dce4"},"parent":{"uid":"chassis","body":"body"},"pos":[0,0.15,3.9],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"mastB","type":"block","name":"Mast 2","params":{"w":1.2,"h":12,"d":0.8,"material":"plastic","color":"#d8dce4"},"parent":{"uid":"chassis","body":"body"},"pos":[0,0.15,-3.9],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"deck","type":"plate","name":"Top deck","params":{"w":7,"h":0.3,"d":9,"material":"plastic","color":"#8fa3b8"},"parent":{"uid":"mastF","body":"body"},"pos":[0,12.15,-3.9],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"battery","type":"battery-18650","name":"Batteries","params":{"count":"2","charge":100},"parent":{"uid":"deck","body":"body"},"pos":[0,0.15,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"brain","type":"maker-board","name":"Brain","params":{"usb":false},"parent":{"uid":"chassis","body":"body"},"pos":[0,0.15,0],"rot":[0,-0.7071,0,0.7071]},{"uid":"driver","type":"drv8833","name":"Motor driver","params":{},"parent":{"uid":"battery","body":"body"},"pos":[0,2,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"imu","type":"mpu6050","name":"MPU-6050","params":{},"parent":{"uid":"chassis","body":"body"},"pos":[2.6,0.15,2.4],"rot":[0,0,0,1]}],"wires":[{"id":"w1","a":{"uid":"battery","pin":"+"},"b":{"uid":"driver","pin":"VM"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w2","a":{"uid":"battery","pin":"-"},"b":{"uid":"driver","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w3","a":{"uid":"battery","pin":"+"},"b":{"uid":"brain","pin":"VIN"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w4","a":{"uid":"battery","pin":"-"},"b":{"uid":"brain","pin":"GND2"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w5","a":{"uid":"brain","pin":"GP2"},"b":{"uid":"driver","pin":"AIN1"},"color":"#e8c547"},{"id":"w6","a":{"uid":"brain","pin":"GP3"},"b":{"uid":"driver","pin":"AIN2"},"color":"#e8c547"},{"id":"w7","a":{"uid":"brain","pin":"GP5"},"b":{"uid":"driver","pin":"BIN1"},"color":"#4a90e2"},{"id":"w8","a":{"uid":"brain","pin":"GP6"},"b":{"uid":"driver","pin":"BIN2"},"color":"#4a90e2"},{"id":"w9","a":{"uid":"driver","pin":"AOUT1"},"b":{"uid":"motorR","pin":"M+"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w10","a":{"uid":"driver","pin":"AOUT2"},"b":{"uid":"motorR","pin":"M-"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w11","a":{"uid":"driver","pin":"BOUT1"},"b":{"uid":"motorL","pin":"M+"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w12","a":{"uid":"driver","pin":"BOUT2"},"b":{"uid":"motorL","pin":"M-"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w13","a":{"uid":"brain","pin":"3V3"},"b":{"uid":"imu","pin":"VCC"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w14","a":{"uid":"brain","pin":"GND"},"b":{"uid":"imu","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w15","a":{"uid":"brain","pin":"SDA"},"b":{"uid":"imu","pin":"SDA"},"color":"#3cb371"},{"id":"w16","a":{"uid":"brain","pin":"SCL"},"b":{"uid":"imu","pin":"SCL"},"color":"#f2f2f2"}],"programs":{"brain":{"lang":"arduino","source":"// Self-balancing robot. It would fall over on its own: the MPU-6050 feels which way it leans and how\n// fast, and the wheels drive under it to catch it (a PD loop). Push it with Shift + the ball and watch\n// it catch itself. Open the serial monitor and press Plot to see the angle and the motor power.\n#include <Wire.h>\n#include <Adafruit_MPU6050.h>\n\n#define AIN1 2   // right motor (through the DRV8833)\n#define AIN2 3\n#define BIN1 5   // left motor\n#define BIN2 6\n\nAdafruit_MPU6050 mpu;\n\nfloat Kp = 35;     // power per degree of lean\nfloat Kd = 1.4;    // power per degree/second of falling\nfloat Ks = 10;     // rolling away: lean against it (so it comes back instead of speeding off)\nfloat angle = 0;   // lean, degrees: + = leaning back\nfloat speed = 0;   // how fast it's rolling (a guess from the power it gives)\nunsigned long last;\nint n = 0;\n\nvoid motor(int in1, int in2, int p) {\n  p = constrain(p, -255, 255);\n  if (p >= 0) { analogWrite(in1, p); analogWrite(in2, 0); }\n  else        { analogWrite(in1, 0); analogWrite(in2, -p); }\n}\n\nvoid drive(int p) {\n  motor(BIN1, BIN2, p);\n  motor(AIN2, AIN1, p);   // the right motor faces the other way\n}\n\nvoid setup() {\n  Serial.begin(115200);\n  Wire.begin();\n  if (!mpu.begin()) {\n    Serial.println(\"No MPU-6050: check its wires\");\n    while (true) delay(100);\n  }\n  mpu.setGyroRange(MPU6050_RANGE_500_DEG);\n  last = micros();\n  Serial.println(\"balancing\");\n}\n\nvoid loop() {\n  sensors_event_t a, g, temp;\n  mpu.getEvent(&a, &g, &temp);\n  float dt = (micros() - last) / 1000000.0;\n  last = micros();\n\n  // the lean from gravity (steady, but fooled while the wheels speed up) and from the gyro (fast but\n  // drifts): mostly the gyro, nudged by gravity\n  float accAngle = atan2(a.acceleration.x, a.acceleration.z) * 180 / PI;\n  float rate = -g.gyro.y * 180 / PI;\n  angle = 0.995 * (angle + rate * dt) + 0.005 * accAngle;\n\n  if (abs(angle) > 40) {   // fallen over: stop the wheels\n    drive(0);\n    speed = 0;\n    return;\n  }\n  float target = Ks * speed * 0.01;   // (lean against rolling off)\n  float power = -(Kp * (angle - target) + Kd * rate);\n  speed = 0.95 * speed + 0.05 * power;\n  drive(power);\n\n  if (++n % 10 == 0) {\n    Serial.print(\"angle:\");\n    Serial.print(angle);\n    Serial.print(\" power:\");\n    Serial.println(power / 10);\n  }\n  delay(4);\n}\n"}},"boards":[]}},{"name":"Compass and tilt alarm","description":"A compass prints which way it faces and a tilt switch sounds the alarm LED. Pick the little board up with the hand: turn it (Q / E) and the heading changes; tip it over and the LED lights.","project":{"format":"bench-workshop","version":1,"name":"Compass and tilt alarm","parts":[{"uid":"board","type":"maker-board","name":"Board","params":{"usb":true},"parent":null,"pos":[-10,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"base","type":"plate","name":"Sensor board","params":{"w":8,"h":0.3,"d":6,"material":"plastic","color":"#f2c230"},"parent":null,"pos":[6,0.15,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"compass","type":"motion-sensors/compass","name":"Compass","params":{},"parent":{"uid":"base","body":"body"},"pos":[-2,0.15,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"tilt","type":"motion-sensors/tilt-switch","name":"Tilt switch","params":{},"parent":{"uid":"base","body":"body"},"pos":[2,0.15,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"led","type":"led","name":"Alarm LED","params":{"color":"red"},"parent":null,"pos":[-10,0,7],"rot":[0,0,0,1]}],"wires":[{"id":"w1","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"3V3"},"b":{"uid":"compass","pin":"VCC"},"color":"#e04848","length":40},{"id":"w2","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND"},"b":{"uid":"compass","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33","length":40},{"id":"w3","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"SDA"},"b":{"uid":"compass","pin":"SDA"},"color":"#3cb371","length":40},{"id":"w4","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"SCL"},"b":{"uid":"compass","pin":"SCL"},"color":"#f2f2f2","length":40},{"id":"w5","a":{"uid":"compass","pin":"VCC"},"b":{"uid":"tilt","pin":"VCC"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w6","a":{"uid":"compass","pin":"GND"},"b":{"uid":"tilt","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w7","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP2"},"b":{"uid":"tilt","pin":"DO"},"color":"#e8c547","length":40},{"id":"w8","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP15"},"b":{"uid":"led","pin":"A"},"color":"#e8c547"},{"id":"w9","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND2"},"b":{"uid":"led","pin":"K"},"color":"#2b2d33"}],"programs":{"board":{"lang":"arduino","source":"// Compass and tilt alarm. Pick the yellow sensor board up (drag it), turn it with Q / E: the heading\n// changes. Tip it over (or drop it on its side) and the alarm LED lights.\n#include <Wire.h>\n#include <QMC5883LCompass.h>\n\n#define TILT 2\n#define ALARM 15\n\nQMC5883LCompass compass;\n\nvoid setup() {\n  Serial.begin(115200);\n  Wire.begin();\n  compass.init();\n  pinMode(TILT, INPUT);\n  pinMode(ALARM, OUTPUT);\n}\n\nvoid loop() {\n  compass.read();\n  int heading = compass.getAzimuth();\n  if (heading < 0) heading += 360;\n  char dir[3];\n  compass.getDirection(dir, heading);\n\n  bool tipped = digitalRead(TILT) == HIGH;\n  digitalWrite(ALARM, tipped ? HIGH : LOW);\n\n  Serial.print(\"heading \");\n  Serial.print(heading);\n  Serial.print(\" deg (\");\n  Serial.print(dir[0]);\n  Serial.print(dir[1]);\n  Serial.print(dir[2]);\n  Serial.print(\")\");\n  if (tipped) Serial.print(\"  TIPPED OVER!\");\n  Serial.println();\n  delay(300);\n}\n"}},"boards":[]}}]}